    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Junior Caminero**, whose 70.76 efficiency score leads the team against Ray. While the park factors in that matchup are slightly punitive, **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from the matchup against a high-xERA starter, positioning him as our premier UTIL option. Close behind is **Kyle Schwarber**, whose leadoff role against Kikuchi generates an elite 70.15 score; the combination of the top-of-the-order advantage and a favorable platoon matchup makes **Kyle Schwarber** our most reliable source of run production today. We are also leaning heavily into **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.10) and **Christian Yelich** (67.69), as both benefit from dynamic platoon advantages that inflate their projections against their respective right-handed opponents.\n\nOur roster construction prioritizes speed and situational efficiency, which necessitated a difficult decision regarding the bench. **Hector Rodriguez** was the closest to cracking the starting lineup with a score of 40.54, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench due to the unfavorable left-on-left dynamic against Imanaga and a suppressed eighth-spot batting order. We are also keeping a close watch on **Colt Keith**; while his 50.07 score remains above our floor, the matchup against Glasnow is our highest risk point of the day, as the elite opposing starter creates significant downward pressure on his raw efficiency. We remain cautious of **Yordan Alvarez**\u2014despite his elite xwOBA\u2014because the left-on-left platoon disadvantage against Thornton has lowered his ceiling compared to the rest of the starting nine. As we hunt for every stolen base, we trust that this lineup\u2019s blend of high-OBP leadoff hitters and optimized platoon positioning will sustain our Roto standing throughout the day.",
